<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">French protectorate of Cambodia</h1><p class="st-meta">1863 CE – 1953 CE · capital Phnom Penh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Cambodia under French protection for ninety years, which saved the kingdom from partition by Siam and Vietnam but subordinated its monarchy to colonial rule.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1863 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-of-cambodia">King Norodom</a>, weakened by Siamese overlordship and internal rivals, signed a treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> accepting a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, partly to escape Siamese pressure. A convention in 1884 forced on him much tighter French control, provoking a rebellion from 1885 to 1887.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>French résidents controlled finance, taxation and administration, while the king kept ritual authority. The capital was moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phnom-penh">Phnom Penh</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> rebuilt. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">Rubber</a> plantations and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> exports grew, but most Cambodians remained farmers, and Vietnamese clerks staffed much of the administration. In 1907 France obtained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battambang">Battambang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siem-reap">Siem Reap</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a>, from Siam. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970">Cambodia</a> became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-indochina">French Indochina</a> in 1887.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan's</a> coup of March 1945 allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">King Norodom Sihanouk</a> to proclaim the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kampuchea-1945">Kingdom of Kampuchea</a>, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> returned that autumn. Sihanouk's 'royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a>' for independence succeeded in November 1953, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/post-angkorian-cambodia">Kingdom of Cambodia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-protectorate-of-cambodia.jpg" alt="French protectorate of Cambodia" width="320" height="206"><figcaption>Image: Vectorization: Mrmw · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cambodia_(1863-1940).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1863 CE – 1953 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Phnom Penh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Norodom, Sisowath, Norodom Sihanouk</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Khmer, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cambodia">Cambodia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Cambodia (protectorate), Cambodge, Kingdom of Cambodia (1863-1953)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1908&amp;focus=french-protectorate-of-cambodia" aria-label="French protectorate of Cambodia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7566 1746 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French protectorate of Cambodia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7886 2002L7880 1991M7886 2002L5054 728M7886 2002L7939 2031M7886 2002L5054 728M7886 2002L7886 2002M7886 2002L7886 2002"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7880 1991h0M5054 728h0M7939 2031h0M5054 728h0M7886 2002h0M7886 2002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7886 2002h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7886 2002h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Phnom Penh. <a href="/atlas?year=1908&amp;focus=french-protectorate-of-cambodia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
